    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Trea Turner** (76.61) stands as our premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Holmes and a favorable spot at the top of the order. He is the clear anchor of the lineup, offering the highest efficiency ceiling among our active roster. **Kazuma Okamoto** (70.30) and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (69.32) are secondary pillars; both hitters are in prime positions to capitalize on park factors and manageable matchups against Jacob Lopez and Cantillo, respectively. While we are waiting on official lineups for **Kazuma Okamoto**, the projected fifth-spot placement remains an elite environment for his power profile. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (60.47) remains a high-priority start despite platoon concerns; his high-efficiency profile on the basepaths against the slower delivery of Gasser makes him a must-start in our pursuit of scarce stolen bases.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision of the day was **Dillon Dingler** (36.60), who fell just shy of our 40.0 efficiency floor. While he provides decent utility, the combination of a difficult matchup against Ryan and a negative platoon split forced him to the bench in favor of higher-ceiling options like **Caleb Durbin** (64.78). We are also navigating a few lineup-dependent variables with **Josh Smith** and **Hector Rodriguez**; both are currently projected for the lineup, but their final efficiency scores could shift if they are moved down in their respective orders. Keep an eye on **Christian Yelich**, whose score (52.41) is hampered by an elite hold pitcher and a platoon disadvantage, though he retains enough value to justify his spot given the current depth. With **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, and **Chase Meidroth** sidelined today, we are counting on the aforementioned starters to shoulder the load and maintain our Roto standing.",
